WEBVTT

00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:34.466
That's defuse as in defusing a bomb.

00:35:34.490 --> 00:35:36.346
The first defusing session Chris did

00:35:36.370 --> 00:35:40.410
was for a crew that just responded
to an emergency call involving an infant.

00:35:40.434 --> 00:35:44.226
You could see how much more helpful it was
than the old debriefing model.

00:35:44.250 --> 00:35:46.149
CM: I just asked them what they needed.

00:35:46.173 --> 00:35:49.616
And so, a couple just wanted
to remain out of service.

00:35:49.640 --> 00:35:51.195
They wanted to call their wives,

00:35:51.219 --> 00:35:52.947
but they all wanted to stay at work,

00:35:52.971 --> 00:35:54.710
because that was that cohesive unit

00:35:54.734 --> 00:35:56.466
and where their support network was.

00:35:56.490 --> 00:36:00.186
But the ambulance crew asked
if they could just go to sleep.